# Session memory (keep Cursor fast)

Chat does not survive session switches. **Do not** force-read `AGENT_HANDOFF.md`,
`ONBOARDING.md`, or other large docs at session start or before every tool call.

## Cursor speed (owner rule)

- A compact on-demand board (`AGENT_HANDOFF.md` ≤ 200 lines) is fine.
- Cursor slows when **alwaysApply** rules force-load huge files every turn.
- Prefer: **git history** + open the board only when in-flight / blocked / locks matter.
- Keep `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` as a **board**, never a changelog.

Full protocol: `SESSION_MEMORY.md`. `CLAUDE.md` already loads automatically.

## When to open docs

| Need | Open |
|---|---|
| In-flight / blocked / file locks | `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` |
| Domain math / non-obvious contracts | `ONBOARDING.md` |
| Fraud / Fiat / KYC | `docs/ANTIFRAUD_CONTRACTS.md` + `.cursor/rules/antifraud.mdc` |

## Before DONE (substantive work only)

1. Update `AGENT_HANDOFF.md` only for open in-flight, blocked, or locks — delete entries when work lands.
2. Promote durable facts to `ONBOARDING.md` or `CLAUDE.md` (binding rules).
3. Never leave task state only in chat. Skip for pure Q&A with zero new facts / zero code changes.

## Sub-agents

Brief with board semantics (in-flight / locks / blocked). Do not require reading the full handoff before tools.
